#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:8
msgid "Using quality-of-service settings for lossy networks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:12
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr "目录"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:15
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:17
msgid ""
"Please read the documentation page :doc:`about QoS settings </ROS-Framework/"
"interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings>` for background "
"information on available support in ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:19
msgid ""
"In this demo, we will spawn a node that publishes a camera image and another "
"that subscribes to the image and shows it on the screen. We will then "
"simulate a lossy network connection between them and show how different "
"quality of service settings handle the bad link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:24
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:25
msgid ""
"This tutorial assumes you have a :doc:`working ROS 2 installation "
"<../../../../Get-Started/Installation>` and OpenCV. See the `OpenCV "
"documentation <http://docs.opencv.org/doc/tutorials/introduction/"
"table_of_content_introduction/table_of_content_introduction.html#table-of-"
"content-introduction>`__ for its installation instructions. You will also "
"need the ROS package ``image_tools``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:31
msgid "Linux Binaries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:33
msgid "$ sudo apt-get install ros-rolling-image-tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:37
msgid "From Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:39
msgid ""
"Clone and build the demos repo using the branch that matches your "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:41
msgid "$ git clone https://github.com/ros2/demos.git -b rolling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:47
msgid "Run the demo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:49
msgid ""
"Before running the demo, make sure you have a working webcam connected to "
"your computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:51
msgid "Once you've installed ROS 2, source your setup file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:55
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:57
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:63
msgid "$ . <path to ROS 2 install space>/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:61
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:67
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:69
msgid "$ call <path to ROS 2 install space>/local_setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:73
msgid "Then run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:75
msgid "$ ros2 run image_tools showimage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:79
msgid ""
"Nothing will happen yet. ``showimage`` is a subscriber node that is waiting "
"for a publisher on the ``image`` topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:82
msgid ""
"Note: you have to close the ``showimage`` process with ``Ctrl-C`` later. You "
"can't just close the window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:85
msgid ""
"In a separate terminal, source the install file and run the publisher node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:87
msgid "$ ros2 run image_tools cam2image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:91
msgid ""
"This will publish an image from your webcam. In case you don't have a camera "
"attached to your computer, there is a commandline option which publishes "
"predefined images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:95
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run image_tools cam2image --ros-args -p burger_mode:=True\n"
"[INFO] [1715662452.055277255] [cam2image]: Publishing image #1\n"
"[INFO] [1715662452.119336061] [cam2image]: Publishing image #2\n"
"[INFO] [1715662452.187315139] [cam2image]: Publishing image #3\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:103
msgid ""
"A window will pop up with the title \"view\" showing your camera feed. In "
"the first window, you'll see output from the subscriber:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:106
msgid ""
"[INFO] [1715662452.188906764] [showimage]: Received image #camera_frame\n"
"Received image #camera_frame\n"
"[INFO] [1715662452.252836919] [showimage]: Received image #camera_frame\n"
"Received image #camera_frame\n"
"[INFO] [1715662452.320878578] [showimage]: Received image #camera_frame\n"
"Received image #camera_frame\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:118
msgid ""
"macOS users: If these examples do not work or you receive an error like "
"``ddsi_conn_write failed -1`` then you'll need to increase your system wide "
"UDP packet size:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:120
msgid ""
"$ sudo sysctl -w net.inet.udp.recvspace=209715\n"
"$ sudo sysctl -w net.inet.udp.maxdgram=65500"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:125
msgid ""
"These changes will not persist a reboot. If you want the changes to persist, "
"add these lines to ``/etc/sysctl.conf`` (create the file if it doesn't exist "
"already):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:128
msgid ""
"net.inet.udp.recvspace=209715\n"
"net.inet.udp.maxdgram=65500"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:134
msgid "Command line options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:136
msgid "In one of your terminals, add a -h flag to the original command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:139
msgid "$ ros2 run image_tools showimage -h"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:146
msgid "Add network traffic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:150
msgid ""
"This section of the demo won't work on RTI's Connext DDS and Fast-DDS. When "
"running multiple nodes in the same host, those DDS implementations use "
"shared memory along with the loopback interface. Degrading the loopback "
"interface throughput won't affect shared memory, thus traffic between the "
"two nodes won't be affected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:156
msgid "This next section is Linux-specific."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:158
msgid ""
"However, for macOS and Windows you can achieve a similar effect with the "
"utilities \"Network Link Conditioner\" (part of the xcode tool suite) and "
"`\"Clumsy\" <http://jagt.github.io/clumsy/index.html>`_, respectively, but "
"they will not be covered in this tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:160
msgid ""
"We are going to use the Linux network traffic control utility, ``tc`` (`man "
"page <http://linux.die.net/man/8/tc>`_) ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:162
msgid "$ sudo tc qdisc add dev lo root netem loss 5%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:166
msgid ""
"This magical incantation will simulate 5% packet loss over the local "
"loopback device. If you use a higher resolution of the images (e.g. ``--ros-"
"args -p width:=640 -p height:=480``) you might want to try a lower packet "
"loss rate (e.g. ``1%``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:169
msgid ""
"Next we start the ``cam2image`` and ``showimage``, and we'll soon notice "
"that both programs seem to have slowed down the rate at which images are "
"transmitted. This is caused by the behavior of the default QoS settings. "
"Enforcing reliability on a lossy channel means that the publisher (in this "
"case, ``cam2image``) will resend the network packets until it receives "
"acknowledgement from the consumer (i.e. ``showimage``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:173
msgid ""
"Let's now try running both programs, but with more suitable settings. First "
"of all, we'll use the ``-p reliability:=best_effort`` option to enable best "
"effort communication. The publisher will now just attempt to deliver the "
"network packets, and don't expect acknowledgement from the consumer. We see "
"now that some of the frames on the ``showimage`` side were dropped, so the "
"frame numbers in the shell running ``showimage`` won't be consecutive "
"anymore:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:179
msgid "Best effort image transfer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:184
msgid "When you're done, remember to delete the queueing discipline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Quality-of-Service.rst:186
msgid "$ sudo tc qdisc delete dev lo root netem loss 5%"
msgstr ""
